        <p class="dek">The National Institutes of Health has confirmed that no conventional topical treatment truly works against nail fungus. A Nashville physician says that has nothing to do with bad luck. It comes down to biology, and almost no one has been told about it.</p>
        <p class="byline">By Staff Writer &middot; Health Desk &middot; <span id="byline-date">July 20, 2026</span> &middot; <span id="read-time">9 min read</span></p>
      </div>

      <figure class="figure-bleed">
        <img
          src="img-adv_01.png"
          alt="Placeholder for hero photo: a rustic wooden kitchen table with an old bottle of apple cider vinegar, a small bottle of oil, fresh herbs, garlic, and a handwritten recipe card in warm morning light. (Replace with hero.jpg)"
